# Unity Prefab Rules

- Prefabs are the primary unit for reusable objects (creatures, props, UI widgets).
- Do not assume objects exist only in the current scene; support prefab instantiation and pooling.
- `PoolManager` uses prefabs for spawn/despawn; ensure prefabs are self-contained (no scene-only references).
- Creature parts can reference prefabs via `CreaturePartDef.ModelPrefab` when using Blender-sourced models.
